#!/bin/bash
# HTTP status 418 is real (RFC 2324). Look it up when you're back on the internet.
cat <<'EOF'
             ;,'
     _o_    ;:;'
 ,-.'---`.__ ;
((j`=====',-'
 `-\     /
    `-=-'     Error 418: I'm a teapot.

I can't brew coffee. I am, fundamentally, a teapot. This is an actual
official internet error code, invented as an April Fools' joke in 1998.
Some real websites still return it.
EOF
